      <h2 id="related">Where to go next</h2>
      <p>If you are hiring courts because you are setting a club up from scratch, the venue is one of five things you need at once. <a href="/guides/how-to-start-a-badminton-club">How to start a badminton club</a> covers the others - players, kit, fees and your first sessions.</p>
      <p>Once the hall is booked, the cost per player depends entirely on how full the courts are. <a href="/guides/fair-court-time-busy-club-night">Giving everyone fair court time on a busy night</a> deals with the sit-out problem directly, and <a href="/guides/how-to-run-a-badminton-club-night">the complete organiser's checklist</a> covers the rest of the evening.</p>
      <p>And the next question after "what does the hall cost" is usually "what do we charge for it". That one has its own answer and its own arithmetic, and it is the guide we are writing next.</p>

      <div style="margin-top:34px;padding-top:22px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)">
        <h4 style="margin:0 0 8px">How this guide was put together</h4>
        <p style="color:var(--muted-2);font-size:.95rem;margin:0">ePegboard builds club-night software. We do not hire out courts, and we are not tax advisers. The prices here come from a survey we ran ourselves: on 26 August 2026 we read the published rate cards and booking pages of 22 UK venues and recorded every figure, with its source. Eighteen sell a comparable per-court unit and those are the ones in the chart. The VAT section is compiled from HMRC's published guidance, and where the treatment depends on your supplier we have said so rather than picking the answer that sounds most useful.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--muted-2);font-size:.95rem;margin:12px 0 0">Where we could not find a source, we have said that too: no operator publishes its block-booking terms, no published figure exists for what clubs actually negotiate off list price, and we found no published badminton rate at any Northern Ireland venue.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--muted-2);font-size:.95rem;margin:12px 0 0"><strong>Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.gov.uk/guidance/vat-on-land-and-property-notice-742" target="_blank" rel="noopener">HMRC, VAT on land and property (Notice 742)</a> &middot; <a href="https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sport-supplies-that-are-vat-exempt-notice-70145" target="_blank" rel="noopener">HMRC, Sport supplies that are VAT exempt (Notice 701/45)</a> &middot; <a href="https://www.sportengland.org/how-we-can-help/facilities-and-planning/planning-for-sport/community-use-agreements" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sport England on community use agreements</a> &middot; <a href="https://www.sportengland.org/guidance-and-support/facilities-and-planning/design-and-cost-guidance/sports-halls" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sport England sports halls design guidance</a> &middot; <a href="https://modgov.sefton.gov.uk/documents/s134842/Fees%20and%20Charges%202026-27%20-%20Sports%20V1.3.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sefton Council fees and charges 2026-27</a> &middot; <a href="https://tdcdemocracy.tendringdc.gov.uk/documents/s74469/Schedule%20of%20Fees%20and%20Charges.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Tendring District Council schedule of fees and charges</a> &middot; <a href="https://councillors.halton.gov.uk/documents/s78625/Appendix%20A%20Sports%20Service%20fees%20and%20charges%202025.26.docx.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Halton Borough Council sports fees 2025/26</a></p>
